    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/0807.3010v25</id>
    <title>Some conjectures on addition and multiplication of complex (real) numbers</title>
    <updated>2008-11-21T02:40:47Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/0807.3010v25" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/0807.3010v25" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  We discuss conjectures related to the following two conjectures:
  (1) for each complex numbers x_1,...,x_n there exist rationals y_1,...,y_n \in [-2^{n-1},2^{n-1}] such that
  \forall i \in {1,...,n} (x_i=1 \Rightarrow y_i=1)
  \forall i,j,k \in {1,...,n} (x_i+x_j=x_k \Rightarrow y_i+y_j=y_k)
  (2) for each complex (real) numbers x_1,...,x_n there exist complex (real) numbers y_1,...,y_n such that
  \forall i \in {1,...,n} |y_i| \leq 2^{2^{n-2}}
  \forall i \in {1,...,n} (x_i=1 \Rightarrow y_i=1)
  \forall i,j,k \in {1,...,n} (x_i+x_j=x_k \Rightarrow y_i+y_j=y_k)
  \forall i,j,k \in {1,...,n} (x_i \cdot x_j=x_k \Rightarrow y_i \cdot y_j=y_k)</summary>
