    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0702558v86</id>
    <title>Bounds of some real (complex) solution of a finite system of polynomial equations with rational coefficients</title>
    <updated>2009-12-04T18:42:21Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0702558v86" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0702558v86" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  We discuss two conjectures.
  (I) For each x_1,...,x_n \in R (C) there exist y_1,...,y_n \in R (C) such that
  \forall i \in {1,...,n} |y_i| \leq 2^{2^{n-2}}
  \forall i \in {1,...,n} (x_i=1 \Rightarrow y_i=1)
  \forall i,j,k \in {1,...,n} (x_i+x_j=x_k \Rightarrow y_i+y_j=y_k)
  \forall i,j,k \in {1,...,n} (x_i \cdot x_j=x_k \Rightarrow y_i \cdot y_j=y_k)
  (II) Let G be an additive subgroup of C. Then for each x_1,...,x_n \in G there exist y_1,...,y_n \in G \cap Q such that
  \forall i \in {1,...,n} |y_i| \leq 2^{n-1}
  \forall i \in {1,...,n} (x_i=1 \Rightarrow y_i=1)
  \forall i,j,k \in {1,...,n} (x_i+x_j=x_k \Rightarrow y_i+y_j=y_k)</summary>
