    <summary>Let E_n={x_i=1, x_i+x_j=x_k, x_i \cdot x_j=x_k: i,j,k \in {1,...,n}}. If Matiyasevich's conjecture on single-fold Diophantine representations is true, then for every computable function f:N-&gt;N there is a positive integer m(f) such that for each integer n&gt;=m(f) there exists a system U \subseteq E_n which has exactly f(n) solutions in non-negative integers x_1,...,x_n.</summary>
